<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0" xmlns:miniflux="https://miniflux.app/opml">
    <head>
        <title>Miniflux</title>
        <dateCreated>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:37:14 UTC</dateCreated>
    </head>
    <body>
        <outline text="void-forks">
            <outline title="AbeirOS" text="AbeirOS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/abeiros/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from AbeirOS Like AgarimOS and AfagOS, AbeirOS is based on Void Linux, and it&amp;#39;s created using void-mklive:&#xD;&#xA;https://github.com/void-linux/void-mklive&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;AbeirOS uses the musl C library, with its pros and cons.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;It includes a minimum set of applications (all included in the official repositories) so you can build your system on your own.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;There are two users:&#xD;&#xA;anon&#xD;&#xA;root&#xD;&#xA;In both cases, the password is voidlinux&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Installation: Type sudo void-installer in a terminal.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The prompt configuration was taken from Venom Linux.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;IMPORTANT:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Never perform a partial update of the Qt6 libraries. Wait until all updates are available (including those packages that need to be recompiled).&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Licensing: According to every single license (in some cases unset) from every single component used. All the license files remain unmodified.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;For more details:&#xD;&#xA;https://linktr.ee/agarimos" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="AfagOS" text="AfagOS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/afagos/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from AfagOS AfagOS translates to &amp;#34;caresses&amp;#34; in English. It conveys a sense of gentle touch, care, and affection, which is a fitting name for a distro that aims to provide a smooth, pleasant, and user-friendly experience.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA; AfagOS is created using void-mklive:&#xD;&#xA;https://github.com/void-linux/void-mklive&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;It includes a minimum set of applications (all included in the official repositories) so you can build your system on your own.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;There are two users:&#xD;&#xA;anon&#xD;&#xA;root&#xD;&#xA;In both cases, the password is voidlinux&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Installation: Type sudo void-installer in a terminal.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The prompt configuration was taken from Venom Linux.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;IMPORTANT:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Never perform a partial update of the Qt6 libraries. Wait until all updates are available (including those packages that need to be recompiled).&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Licensing: According to every single license (in some cases unset) from every single component used. All the license files remain unmodified.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;For more details:&#xD;&#xA;https://linktr.ee/agarimos" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="AgarimOS" text="AgarimOS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/agarimos/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from AgarimOS Please note that AgarimOS is a personal project, I just want to learn how GNU Linux works. The same applies to AfagOS and AbeirOS.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;AgarimOS is created using void-mklive:&#xD;&#xA;https://github.com/void-linux/void-mklive&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;It includes a minimum set of applications (all included in the official repositories)  so you can build your system on your own.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;KDE Plasma is the main desktop.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Like in the official Void Linux ISO, there are two users:&#xD;&#xA;anon&#xD;&#xA;root&#xD;&#xA;In both cases, the password is voidlinux&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Installation: &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Like a regular Void Linux install, type sudo void-installer in a terminal.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Demonstration: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aKdHNavm40I (AgarimOS)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Groups selection matters!! So please choose the groups you will need!!&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;For more details:&#xD;&#xA;https://linktr.ee/agarimos&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Licensing: According to every single license (in some cases unset) from every single component used. All the license files remain unmodified." miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="BRGV-OS" text="BRGV-OS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/brgv-os/rss?path=/brgv-os/en_US" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from BRGV-OS BRGV-OS is a Linux distribution based on Void Linux, with packages manager xbps.  ISO files is in brgv-os directory.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The work was do it for our job needs (Gene Bank research institute from Suceava, Romania), but anyone can modify for their needs. &#xD;&#xA;The name BRGV mean in Romanian &amp;#34;Banca de Resurse Genetice Vegetale&amp;#34; (shortly in English is Gene Bank), an OS mean of course Operating System. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Starting with release 23092026 introduces two distinct hardware profiles: a Generic stable ISO and a highly tailored edition optimized specifically for Slimbook EVO laptops running AMD Strix Point architectures." miniflux:blockFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).sha256" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="Cereus Linux" text="Cereus Linux" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/cereus-linux/rss?path=/isos" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from Cereus Linux" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="d77void" text="d77void" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/d77void/rss?path=/ISO-x86_64" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from d77void What is d77void GNU/Linux?&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;It&amp;#39;s a respin of Void GNU/Linux, created to demonstrate the capabilities of Void&amp;#39;s tools, such as void-mklive and void-packages. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Originally initiated as a Void respin with Fluxbox it has evolved to offer a wide range of options, including the window managers awesome, bspwm, dwm, fluxbox, herbstluftwm, hyprland, i3wm, JWM, labwc, leftwm, mangowc, niri, openbox, qtile, river, sway, wayfire and the desktop environments  Gnome, LXQt, Plasma and XFCE.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Two user accounts are provided: anon and root, both with the password &amp;#39;voidlinux&amp;#39;. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The distribution can be installed using Calamares.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Finally decided to create org at github; if you wish to contribute, find the project at https://github.com/d77void&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Check out my other project https://hybrid-d77.sourceforge.io&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;To support my work contribute here: https://buymeacoffee.com/d77void" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="Release notes from EclipseLinux" text="Release notes from EclipseLinux" xmlUrl="https://github.com/TheCodeVerseHub/EclipseLinux/releases.atom" htmlUrl="https://github.com/TheCodeVerseHub/EclipseLinux/releases" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="F-Void" text="F-Void" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/f-void/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from F-Void F-Void (Fork of Void) is a mild modification of Void Linux, its main differences are these:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;-You can choose the CLI installer or the Calamares installer&#xD;&#xA;-It comes with 3 desktop types (LXQT, CDE and icewm).&#xD;&#xA;-Changed Firefox to Libre Wolf, Brave and otter-browser-1.0.81_1&#xD;&#xA;-Brought as an alternative manager to Midnight commander, double.commander-1.0.6beta.rev-120_1&#xD;&#xA;-The jdownloader-2_2 is integrated in the system.&#xD;&#xA;-Text editors include these four: xed-editor-3.2.4_1, FeatherPad-1.3.0_1 , Leafpad and Notepadpp&#xD;&#xA;-It already comes with the latest version of Wine.&#xD;&#xA;-For p2p it comes with the latest version of Amule and transmission-bt uses the QT version.&#xD;&#xA;-7zip with its original graphical interface for managing compressed files.&#xD;&#xA;-Added an icon of Linux Void logos in the toolbar.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;-Includes the Abandonware/GPL/Freeware/Donateware games that are native to Linux:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;-SDL-Prince of persia&#xD;&#xA;-Ascension&#xD;&#xA;-Open Tyrian&#xD;&#xA;-Xmoto&#xD;&#xA;-Steel War&#xD;&#xA;-Gemma&#xD;&#xA;-TinyCrate" miniflux:blockFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).xbps" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="gabeeOSLinux" text="gabeeOSLinux" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/gabeeoslinux/rss?path=/Distro" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from gabeeOSLinux GabeeOS is a rolling-release Void-based Linux distribution (spin) , which brings the necessary software to satisfy the daily needs of an end user; in a simple and aesthetically pleasing desktop environment.&#xD;&#xA;gabeeOSLinuxQtile INSTALLER: https://youtu.be/Rs12xKhQua4&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Login to LiveCD:&#xD;&#xA;user: anon&#xD;&#xA;user: root&#xD;&#xA;password: voidlinux&#xD;&#xA;Install: gabeeos-installer&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;SUPR + CONTROL + K: Show Keybindings&#xD;&#xA;SUPR + RETURN: Kitty terminal&#xD;&#xA;SUPR + R: Rofi in WM, Walker in Hyprland&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;gabeeOS Linux Qtile on Youtube:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Channel Ruben_&amp;amp;_Linux&#xD;&#xA;www.youtube.com/embed/p5RzDvwJTuw?rel=0" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="Hybrid-d77" text="Hybrid-d77" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/hybrid-d77/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from Hybrid-d77 What is Hybrid-d77?&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;It&amp;#39;s a respin of Chimera Linux, created to demonstrate the capabilities of Chimera&amp;#39;s tools, such as chimera-live, chimera-install-scripts and cports.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Available only as a proof of concept with Sway as window compositor and my usual configs that you might know from d77void.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Two user accounts are provided: anon and root, both with the password &amp;#39;chimera&amp;#39;.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The distribution can be installed using &amp;#34;doas h77-installer&amp;#34;.&#xD;&#xA;This script is very similar to the one Void uses by default, so for everyone used to Void installer is a well known install method." miniflux:blockFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso.sha256" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="KLV-Airedale" text="KLV-Airedale" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/klv-airedale/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from KLV-Airedale The heart of KLV-Airedale is a &amp;#39;FirstRib&amp;#39; magic initrd which uses overlay filesystem to provide frugal install save persistence, typical load squashfs capabilities (including currently unique ability to load uncompressed physical directories into the layers hierarchy), and copy2ram option. Similarly small sized flexible distros are available such as KLA-OT2base (openbox/tint2 also Arch-based), KLU-jam (Ubuntu-based) and KLV-Airedale (Void Linux based)." miniflux:blockFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).txt" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="KLV-Spectr" text="KLV-Spectr" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/klv-spectr/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from KLV-Spectr KLV-Spectr is one branch of the Kennel Linux (KLV) project — a family of Void Linux respins built by regulars on the Puppy Linux forum. Its sibling, KLV-Airedale, runs a conventional XFCE desktop; Spectr swaps that for spectrwm, aimed at people who already know they&amp;#39;d rather tile than drag. The desktop layer and theming is maintained by Sofiya, with the spectrwm keybinding set built out by geo_c, and releases packaged by rockedge using the FirstRib build system." miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="LazyLinux" text="LazyLinux" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/lazylinux/rss?path=/iso" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from LazyLinux LazyLinux is a pre-configured distro from Hadrut, Armenia based on Void Linux featuring XFCE desktop and latest kernel version to provide a stable and user-friendly experience. It comes with a large number of software preinstalled for almost any purpose. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;!!! As of 2025.09.06 there is an  experimental version with cachyos patches.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Installation: calamares or lazy-installer&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;User: anon&#xD;&#xA;Password: lazylinux&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Created with: https://github.com/lazylinuxos/lazylinux-mklive" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="LyargoOS" text="LyargoOS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/lyargoos/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from LyargoOS An opinionated Void Linux-based distribution with preconfigured KDE Plasma desktop, curated applications, and Calamares graphical installer. Built for performance and simplicity." miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="Neko Void" text="Neko Void" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/neko-void/rss?path=/isos" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from Neko Void  🐱 What is Neko-Void? ///DISTRO THERIAN FRIENDLY!!! &#xD;&#xA;Neko-Void is an unofficial respin of Void Linux ( void based distro ) featuring a preconfigured with carefully selected software for a complete out-of-the-box experience. Designed for users who want Void Linux&amp;#39;s stability and minimalism with modern desktop functionality.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;REMEMBER TO DOWNLOAD THE ISO FROM OUR WEBSITE &#xD;&#xA;(WE TAKE A LITTLE WHILE TO UPDATE THIS SOURCEFORGE REPOSITORY)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WEB PAGE= https://www.neko-void-linux.online&#xD;&#xA;DistroWatch: https://distrowatch.com/table.php?distribution=nekovoid     &amp;lt;3&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Donate: https://linktr.ee/javiercplusx&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ISO&amp;#39;s Archives/betas/experimentals= https://archive.org/details/Neko-Void&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Build-iso=https://github.com/Neko-Void-Linux/Neko-Void&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Core System&#xD;&#xA;- Void Linux base (rolling release)&#xD;&#xA;- MATE Desktop fully configured and optimized&#xD;&#xA;- tinyfetch  minimalist system information tool&#xD;&#xA;- UEFI and Legacy BIOS support&#xD;&#xA;- Octoxbps (install apps without terminal)" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="Noid Linux" text="Noid Linux" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/noid-linux/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from Noid Linux Noid Linux is my personal customization of Void Linux. It&amp;#39;s tailored to my preferences and comes with a custom XBPS repository enabled out of the box." miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="PepVoid" text="PepVoid" xmlUrl="https://rssreader.oscloud.cz/api/query.php?user=zenobit&amp;t=6GjgFjCNHb5ELWebqhqyag&amp;f=rss" htmlUrl="https://rssreader.oscloud.cz/api/query.php?user=zenobit&amp;t=6GjgFjCNHb5ELWebqhqyag&amp;f=rss" description="PepVoid" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="ShrikeLinux" text="ShrikeLinux" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/shrikelinux/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from ShrikeLinux ShrikeLinux Arch based distro and Void Based Distro Called ShrikeV &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ShrikeV Login &#xD;&#xA;UserName: shrike&#xD;&#xA; Password:   toor&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Shrike Arch Based&#xD;&#xA;wth xfce4, spectrwm, dk, and i3wm with 3 Linux kernels Regular[rolling], LTS and Zen.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ShrikeV Void Base&#xD;&#xA;xfce4" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="T4n-OS" text="T4n-OS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/t4n-os/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from T4n-OS  T4n OS adalah GNU/Linux berbasis Void Linux, dirancang dengan prinsip minimalis, cepat, dan ringan. Sistem ini menggunakan runit sebagai init system untuk memberikan performa maksimal dan kontrol penuh terhadap sistem.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;T4n OS dikembangkan di Indonesia, Aceh, dan pertama kali diinisiasi oleh Gh0sT4n pada 17 Agustus 2025, seorang pelajar asal Aceh (Darussa’adah Cot Tarom Baroh – SMKN 5 Takengon). Pengembangan T4n OS menggunakan pendekatan community-driven: dari komunitas, oleh komunitas, dan untuk komunitas.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Selain itu, T4n OS mengadopsi konsep repositori yang terinspirasi dari AUR (Arch User Repository), yaitu VUR (Void User Repository), untuk mempermudah distribusi dan pengelolaan paket bagi pengguna. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Repository :&#xD;&#xA;- T4n-Maker (Tools Build OS) : https://github.com/T4n-Labs/t4n-live&#xD;&#xA;- Repo VUR : https://github.com/T4n-Labs/vur&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Informasi Lainnya :&#xD;&#xA;- T4n OS Website : https://T4n-Labs.github.io/t4n-os/&#xD;&#xA;- VUR Web : https://T4n-Labs.github.io/vur-web/" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
            <outline title="VoidJW OS" text="VoidJW OS" xmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net/projects/voidjw/rss?path=/" htmlUrl="https://sourceforge.net" description="Files from VoidJW OS Void Linux con JWM" miniflux:keepFilterEntryRules="EntryTitle=(?i).iso" type="rss"></outline>
        </outline>
    </body>
</opml>
